solstone-linux Rust release install notes

This package contains the solstone app for linux and its canonical icons. It intentionally
does not install a systemd unit: service ownership
belongs to the optional `solstone-linux install-service` command.

Runtime requirements:

- glibc 2.35 or newer
- libpulse and a PulseAudio-compatible server (PipeWire Pulse is supported)
- GStreamer 1.0 core, base, good, PipeWire, and X11 plugins
- PipeWire and xdg-desktop-portal with ScreenCast support for Wayland screen frames
- xdg-utils for opening links
- a desktop notification service; a StatusNotifier host is what shows the panel icon.
  KDE has one. On GNOME, run `solstone-linux panel-icon` after installing this package

Typical package families:

- Debian/Ubuntu: libpulse0, libgstreamer1.0-0,
  gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
  gstreamer1.0-pipewire, gstreamer1.0-x, pipewire-pulse,
  xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-utils
- Fedora/RHEL: pulseaudio-libs, gstreamer1,
  gstreamer1-plugins-base, gstreamer1-plugins-good, pipewire-gstreamer,
  pipewire-pulseaudio, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-utils
- openSUSE: libpulse0, gstreamer, gstreamer-plugins-base,
  gstreamer-plugins-good, gstreamer-plugin-pipewire, pipewire-pulseaudio,
  xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-utils
- Arch: libpulse, gstreamer, gst-plugins-base, gst-plugins-good,
  gst-plugin-pipewire, pipewire-pulse, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-utils

Create a pair link for this device in your journal, save it as
`pair-link.txt`, then pair and start the solstone app:

```bash
solstone-linux install-service
systemctl --user stop solstone-linux
solstone-linux setup < pair-link.txt
systemctl --user start solstone-linux
```

Pairing is the only setup path, including when your journal is on this machine.
There is no URL, key, local installation of the journal or Python, or direct
fallback to configure. The solstone app takes in what you share with it while
unpaired or offline, holding segments on this device until they reach your
journal.

Setup and runtime share one private-state lock. Stop the solstone app before
pairing. If it is running, setup exits before consuming input and leaves intake,
config, and private state unchanged. Use the same stop, setup, start sequence
when an upgrade requires a new pair link.
